bic_trace_step.reason:
The function `erofs_fileio_ki_complete()` in this commit contains the vulnerable logic. Specifically, lines 27-30: 
c
	if (ret >= 0 && ret != rq->bio.bi_iter.bi_size) {
		bio_advance(&rq->bio, ret);
		zero_fill_bio(&rq->bio);
	}

This code incorrectly treats any short read (where `ret >= 0` but is less than the expected size) as a successful read of the completed portion and zero-fills the rest of the bio. It then completes the folios with `ret < 0` as the error indicator (which evaluates to `false` since `ret >= 0`), marking the unread folios as uptodate instead of failing the I/O request.
